  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Categorise the following functions as either even, odd, or neither, and provide reasoning for each answer.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^3-2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Odd: $f(-x)=-f(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)^3-2(-x)\\\\f(-x)&=-x^3+2x\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain is $\\mathbb R$, so $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^4+x^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither: $f(-x)=x^4-x^3$ equals neither $f(x)$ nor $-f(x)$ identically.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)^4+(-x)^3\\\\f(-x)&=x^4-x^3.\\end{align*}$$\nThis is neither $f(x)=x^4+x^3$ nor $-f(x)=-x^4-x^3$ for all $x$. Hence $f$ is neither even nor odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{2x^2-1}{3-x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even: $f(-x)=f(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{2(-x)^2-1}{3-(-x)^2}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{2x^2-1}{3-x^2}\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain excludes $\\pm\\sqrt3$ and is symmetric about $0$. Hence $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{2^x-2^{-x}}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even: both numerator and denominator change sign, so $f(-x)=f(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{2^{-x}-2^x}{-x}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{2^x-2^{-x}}{x}\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain is $x\\ne0$, which is symmetric about $0$. Hence $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x^3}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither: $f(-x)=\\dfrac{x^3}{x-1}$ satisfies neither parity identity.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{(-x)^3}{-x+1}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{x^3}{x-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThis equals neither $f(x)$ nor $-f(x)$ identically. Also, the domain $x\\ne-1$ is not symmetric about $0$. Hence $f$ is neither even nor odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x^3-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even: $f(-x)=f(x)$ on the original domain $x\\ne-1,0,1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{-x}{(-x)^3-(-x)}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{-x}{-(x^3-x)}\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominator is $x(x-1)(x+1)$, so $x\\ne-1,0,1$. This domain is symmetric about $0$, and $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x^2-5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Odd: $f(-x)=-f(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{-x}{(-x)^2-5}\\\\f(-x)&=-\\frac{x}{x^2-5}\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain excludes $\\pm\\sqrt5$ and is symmetric about $0$. Hence $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^3-x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither: $f(-x)=-x^3+x+1$ satisfies neither parity identity.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)^3-(-x)+1\\\\f(-x)&=-x^3+x+1.\\end{align*}$$\nThis is neither $f(x)=x^3-x+1$ nor $-f(x)=-x^3+x-1$ for all $x$. Hence $f$ is neither even nor odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q13-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{3^{2x}+1}{3^x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even: $f(x)=3^x+3^{-x}$, so $f(-x)=f(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=3^x+3^{-x}\\\\f(-x)&=3^{-x}+3^x\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain is $\\mathbb R$, so $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
